# chorus golden vector: stream end, message type 0x03.
#
# Hand written and committed. The test suite reads this file and never writes
# it. Any implementation of the chorus protocol, in any language, must produce
# these exact bytes from the canonical input in stream_end.fields.
#
# Format: whitespace separated hex bytes, '#' starts a comment.

# frame header: type 0x03, payload length 12 (0x000C), big-endian
03 00 0C

# final_sequence = 41, the last chunk the server emitted
00 00 00 29
# end_timestamp_ns = 840000000. The relation is the one docs/protocol.md
# defines and is normative for: the final chunk's timestamp_ns plus one
# configured chunk duration, in ns on the server timeline. Here that is
# 820000000 + 20000000.
00 00 00 00 32 11 62 00
